                <pb facs="0832" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg734"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Baron Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The tidings of the King’s assassination has profoundly shocked public sentiment.
                    The President has telegraphed to His Majesty.Vittorio Emanuele offering in his
                    name and on behalf of the American people sincere condolences in this hour of
                    deep bereavement. Permit me to add the assurances of my personal sympathy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
